<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Web">

  <!--
    Payout.Api (C133, payout-svc) — the weekly driver payout run (AL-58).

    WHY THIS SERVICE EXISTS. AL-57 made MageRide the payee of a card-paid ride: the passenger tops
    up a wallet, the fare moves passenger wallet -> driver wallet, and the driver's balance becomes
    money the platform OWES. AL-05 had deleted the only outward bank rail, so nothing could
    discharge it. This service is that discharge and nothing else — it prices nothing, settles no
    ride, and never decides who may be paid (that is the Verification Officer, through the AL-39
    queue).

    FENCES:
      * Weekly FULL sweep — no minimum, no holdback (`Payout:RetainMinor` defaults to 0).
      * The wallet debit and the `billing.payouts` row are made recoverable rather than atomic:
        they live in two services, so the payout id is DERIVED from (batch, driver) and the ledger
        key from the payout id — a re-run replays the debit and completes the insert. See
        `PayoutIds` for the whole argument.
      * A driver with no VERIFIED `registry.driver_payout_profiles` row accrues and is never swept.
        The balance is retained, never lost.
      * **This service writes no `billing.journal_postings` row.** wallet-svc (C046) is the only
        writer of the ledger on this platform (D-09); the money moves through its
        `/v1/internal/wallet/driver-payout` seam, which the AL-58 change set added.
      * The bank adapter is ONE outbound port and no provider is chosen. Unconfigured, the run
        still selects, still debits and still records what is owed, and says so at start-up.

    ⚠ Origination via LankaPay/CEFTS needs a sponsor bank and CBSL authorisation (ADD §1.18). That
    is a go-live gate, not something this service discharges.

    Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Web: an HTTP surface (backend/contracts/payout.yaml) plus a scheduled runner.

    Verify: dotnet test backend/src/Payout.Api.Tests -c Release
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>MageRide.Payout</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>MageRide.Payout</AssemblyName>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <UserSecretsId>mageride-payout</UserSecretsId>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Dapper, Npgsql, RS256 auth, the RFC 7807 handler and the command log all arrive through
         the kernel. No package of this service's own: the bank adapter is an HttpClient behind an
         interface, and there is no provider to bind to yet. -->
    <ProjectReference Include="..\MageRide.Shared\MageRide.Shared.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Payout.Api.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
